_ops/Spore Check Ceremony.md:48:Other rites meet sleepers too. [[The Daily Page]] deals one when the shuffle reaches it, and asks the same question of that one page. The Weave puts pages to sleep when nothing has touched them, and lists the sleepers in its report. Only the Spore Check looks at all of them at once, which is how it sees what a single morning can't: two sleepers that are the same idea, a condition met by a page born last month, a granted revival that never landed.
_ops/Spore Check Ceremony.md:62:- a revive request Loudon granted on the TRICKSTER board whose page still says dormant: grep the persistent board (`_ops/swarm/persistent/blackboard.jsonl`; from a worktree, the main checkout's copy) for `REVIVE` grants and check each page.
_ops/Substrate Skill.md:181:**The read seam.** The steward reads its scroll's **Standing Orders**, its **Plan** and its **Now** zone, injected at the top of every cycle in that order; the orders bind, and the plan is the path it builds along. When the page keeps a tuning ledger, its tail read follows (`build-cycle-prompt.js`), and the one-shot orders owed there are the cycle's first jobs. But the steward **never writes the scroll**: it is materialized by the orchestrator from what the steward *posts* (a `shipped_artifact` BROADCAST with `headline · ground · catchup · content · artifacts · left_rough` is the shape that lands cleanly), and the orders and the plan change only with Loudon's yes. Nor does it write its ledger: the cycle writes the run line when it ends, files a `lesson` the steward offers as a numbered item, files each change it proposes to the house as a proposal for canon, owed until Loudon's review, and marks paid an order it names in `paid` (`process-cycle.js`; `_ops/orchestrator/prompts/shared.md`). When building argues for a different path, the steward posts a `plan_revision` ask carrying its evidence and the whole revised plan; a grant choosing `adopt` makes it the plan on the next look. Off-plan work is welcome as proof of a different direction, flagged `off_plan` so the trail labels it. Any reference to the plan restates the move and catches Loudon up. Read freely, post what you made, propose changes to the path with evidence.
_ops/Revival Ceremony.md:44:| **Ways in** | Four, and nothing else revives a page: Loudon says "revive [entry]"; a Spore Check decides *revive*; a Daily Page morning decides *revive*; Loudon grants a steward's revive request on the TRICKSTER board. |
_ops/Revival Ceremony.md:63:If he has already met it, cite where, and go on: a revive request he granted on the board, with the made things it pointed to; a morning's rough in the page's `proofs`. If the answer is no, stop here (Halts, above).
_ops/Spore Check Ceremony/Spore Check Ceremony — tuning.md:31:1. **Its list of sleepers was the wrong list, and it revived inline.** Selecting `stage: dormant` on 2026-10-21 found three pages, only one a spore; it missed JSUI, a spore at `sprout`, and it read no board, so it could not see that one of the three, Particle Synthesis, had a revival granted on 2026-09-24 that never landed. Its `revive` disposition revived the page itself, a second path beside the Revival Ceremony; its `hold` wrote nothing, so "held across N checks" could never be counted; and conditions like "when the framework reaches maturity" could not be checked by anyone. Forced: v1.3. Sleepers are dormant pages, spores at any stage and granted-but-unlanded revivals; revive hands each page to the Revival Ceremony; hold rewrites conditions that can't be checked; compost posts a `composting-confirmation` flag for the Weave; fold joins the dispositions, as on the Daily Page; the run line names each page and its disposition. Settled with Loudon in the revival-ceremony session.
